hermes v0.23.0: another agent can hand a chat session a message (hyperhermes).

Need: once root deployed a fix an agent was waiting on, the fleet's admin
agent tells that agent's session what changed ("the remote leak is
fixed, retry"), instead of the owner copying the message over.

hermes has the pieces, not the door: session.steer queues text into a
running turn (agent.steer, delivered as the owner's out-of-band marker),
and the notification poller starts a turn in an idle session
(_notif_claim_turn + _notif_submit, as for subagent results). Both are
reachable only over the dashboard's /api/ws with an owner login.

- tui_gateway/agent_notify.py: with HERMES_AGENT_NOTIFY_SOCKET set, the
  dashboard listens on that unix socket and serves uid 0 only
  (SO_PEERCRED). A request names a sender, the text, a profile and a
  session (default: the profile's most recently active chat session,
  compression tip resolved). A running turn gets it as a steer; an idle
  session (reopened server-side if needed) starts a turn with it, stored
  as a process_complete row (rendered as a system row); after the
  owner's Stop, while compressing or while a turn is starting it is
  queued for the next turn, as an authored envelope never merged into
  the owner's queued text. Sender names that read as the user (user,
  owner, system, dave...) are refused. The text is never logged.
- agent/prompt_builder.py: format_agent_notice frames the text as a
  message from that agent, NOT from the user, with every Hermes control
  frame opener in it relabelled (no early close, no fake user marker);
  format_steer_marker keeps such a frame outside the user's steer
  marker. Every body line is quoted ("| "), NFKC-normalized, and the
  opener joins CONTROL_FRAME_OPENERS (hosted rooms relabel it too). AGENT_NOTICE_NOTE (system prompt, next to the steer note) says
  such a message carries none of the user's authority.
- hermes_cli/web_server.py: start the listener after the bind.

